+## Keys and roles
+
+Every request sends `Authorization: Bearer <key>`. Keys are in the data file
+under `apiKeys` (`docs/DATA.md`); each has a role:
+
+- `viewer`: every `GET` route except `GET /audit`.
+- `cook`: as viewer, plus `POST /recipes/:id/cook`,
+  `POST /batches/:id/waste`, `POST /temperatures` and
+  `POST /stocktakes/:id/counts`.
+- `manager`: every route, including `GET /audit`.
+
+No key or an unknown key answers 401 `unauthorized`; a known key whose role
+may not use the route answers 403 `forbidden`.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every request that is not a `GET` and carries a known key writes an audit
+entry `{ id, at, key, method, path, status }`, whatever its status (`key` is
+the key's name, never the key). `GET /audit` lists them newest first, for
+managers only.
+
 ## Errors

 Errors have a status from `src/errors.js` and the body
